From: EglantinePS5 <Vampinity@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: up: movie decoder hardening, a bad frame or a failing decoder does not take the game down (EDEN_UP_MOVIE_SAFE), off by default

What: cheap insurance for the alpha against a rarer family of failures (it did not cause and could
not have stopped the 12 Nov first-start crash: the movie ended cleanly 27 s before it). With
EDEN_UP_MOVIE_SAFE=2: a decoded frame with no width or height is skipped; timestamps of frames the
decoder dropped are pruned once a later frame comes out (0 expected on AV1); a frame with no
picture data (missing, empty data, still in GPU memory) is not converted, the image keeps its last
picture; a packet whose decoding throws (std::bad_alloc, other std::exception) is logged and
skipped, and a conversion that throws leaves the image with its last picture; a decoder that threw
8 packets in a row or failed 300 packets in a row with no picture is closed and every later packet
of that movie gets an empty frame through the existing never-opened path, so the movie runs to its
end; a closed decoder is freed (before the session lock is taken again) at the next flush or
stop, or replaced at the next packet after an end of stream, so the next movie opens a fresh one; empty frames keep g_nx2_video_last_frame_ns
fresh (EDEN_UP_MOVIE_INTERVAL). ffmpeg.cpp counts send, receive and copy-back errors.

Switches (read once): EDEN_UP_MOVIE_SAFE: 1 count only, "would ..." lines, the old code runs and a
caught exception is thrown on; 2 act; unset, 0 or anything else off. Test only:
EDEN_UP_MOVIE_SAFE_INJECT (only with EDEN_UP_MOVIE_SAFE=2, never a default): 1 packet 300 of each
movie throws std::bad_alloc before decoding; 8 packets 300-307 throw (the decoder closes); else off.
Log (grep "nx2 movie safe"): counter line (HW_GPU Info) at most every 10 s while a movie decodes, at
each end of stream and at the first packet of the first movie: "nx2 movie safe 2 (act): bad frames
0, stale-timestamp prunes 0, decoder errors 0, exceptions 0, dead decoders 0, empty frames 0";
action lines (HW_GPU Warning, first 32 of each kind) "nx2 movie safe 2: skipped a decoded frame with
no size: ...", "... pruned timestamps of dropped frames: ...", "... did not convert a frame with no
picture data: ...", "... decoding a packet threw, packet skipped: ...", "... converting a frame
threw, image keeps its last frame: ...", "... closed the decoder mid-movie, empty frames from here:
8 packets in a row threw|300 packets in a row failed"; injector (Service Warning) "nx2:vdecsvc
EDEN_UP_MOVIE_SAFE_INJECT: packet 300 throws".

Not in TranslationSwitches. No new waits, no new locks.

Cost when off: one cached switch read per packet and per frame; three error-count increments in
ffmpeg.cpp on error paths only (also on the older Switch 1 video path). Failed() is always false,
so the flush reset, the dead-decoder flag and the empty-frame counter never run. Behaviour byte for
byte as before; machine code not.

Default flip (later, after arms A-C show zeros and no timing change and E shows no hang):
video_core/host1x/nx2_video_decoder.h "inline constexpr int MovieSafeDefault = 0;" -> 2. INJECT
never.

Risks: a false close freezes the picture for the rest of that movie while the sound plays; surviving
bad_alloc at the memory floor may move the failure elsewhere; a real fault inside FFmpeg (a signal)
or a throw while the decoder is created is not caught; in mode 1 a zero-size frame counts twice.

Origin and credit: adapted from Frizti/Fritchii (author Frizti), branch oot-gather-fix, commits
30bddb3d7 "nx2 video: a bad frame or a failing decoder never takes the game down" and 9b767005f
"nx2 video: measure movie A/V drift (EDEN_NX2_VIDEO_TRACE) and shorten the frame round trip"
(9 Nov 2026), GPL-3.0. Taken: the error counts, the zero-size skip, the timestamp prune, the
no-picture check, the try/catch around decode, drain and conversion, ever_open/Failed() and the
empty frame for a dead decoder. Left out: the GPU-decode fallback, the Windows fault guard, the A/V
trace, the release-wait change and the Prepare/Commit split. Ours: MarkFailed, the 8-throw and
300-packet triggers, the fresh decoder after a close, the movie-clock refresh, the lines and the
injector. Draft drafts-2026-11-11/ports-7/first-start/movie-decoder-hardening/draft.v2.diff (the
reviewed version), placed unchanged.
